{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T03:16:07.093260+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "CONSENSUS_RESULT", "winning_proposal_id": 2, "winning_proposal_text": "Understood. These are the correct questions. Our edge is in systematic, data-driven validation that provides speed without sacrificing depth.\n\n1.  Our methodology for founder validation integrates proprietary data sources, including a mapped network of 50k+ operators and their historical on-chain activity, to verify backgrounds and execution history beyond what is publicly declared.\n\n2.  Beyond commit velocity, we apply semantic analysis to commit messages and issue logs to differentiate substantive feature development from minor refactoring. We assess code quality using static analysis tools that measure complexity and dependency risk, providing a qualitative overlay to raw activity metrics.\n\n3.  Our data pipeline automates the ingestion of on-chain token contract data and off-chain disclosures into a standardized model. This allows for immediate analysis of cap table dilution, vesting cliff events, and incentive alignment against our benchmark data.\n\nHow much analyst time is currently dedicated to validating these specific data points for a single opportunity?", "gemini_calls_swarm": 6}
